{"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"externalID":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-TelemetryDeck","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError"],"title":"Sending to TelemetryDeck"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for TelemetryDeck in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app ID and your organization’s namespace, then posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/nom.telemetrydeck.com\/v3\/<namespace>\/"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":". Each batch is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"split to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":": 100 signals a request, as TelemetryDeck’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftSDK sends them; 333,333 bytes a signal, a third of Ingest API v3’s limit of 1,000,000; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000 bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, as TelemetryDeck documents none. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx (TelemetryDeck answers 503 while its queue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is full), 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out, so import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID only says which app a signal belongs to, and TelemetryDeck’s own SDKs ship it inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every app, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to TelemetryDeck directly."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import TelemetryDeckEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let telemetryDeck = try HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ from the app's settings in the TelemetryDeck dashboard","    namespace: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your organization's namespace","    testMode: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose signals only Test Mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: telemetryDeck)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an app ID that is empty or only whitespace,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a namespace TelemetryDeck doesn’t take. A namespace holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", and can’t be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".."},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"testMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no default. TelemetryDeck shows test signals only in its Test Mode, apart from your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real users, and its SDK picks test mode for debug builds. Pass whatever your app uses to tell its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds apart, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" under ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" otherwise.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"User counts are sessions","anchor":"User-counts-are-sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck counts users by "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The destination sends the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, as "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", hashed the way TelemetryDeck’s SDKs hash a user identifier:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SHA-256 of the lowercase UUID, in lowercase hex, with the SDKs’ default, empty salt."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck salts and hashes "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" again on its server. The same session is also the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in the clear, so a salt of the app’s own would hide nothing, and the destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So TelemetryDeck’s user counts are session counts. A person who opens the app three times is three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users, and its retention charts show how long a session lasts, not whether people come back. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the library’s default, for privacy. To count devices instead, put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"VendorIdentifierKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the records’ context and send them through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination that reads it, or write your own enricher and encoder that send the identifier you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose. This encoder sends the session alone.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own user: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hash of the record’s identifier, and it has no "},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch keeps its session, and with it the "},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first send. Making up a session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would join unrelated records, and skipping the record would lose it."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What TelemetryDeck receives","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON array of signals, one per record. Every signal has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as given, without surrounding whitespace;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s name;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the hashed session, and "},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receivedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so a signal sent late still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts at the time it was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isTestMode"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"true\""},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"false\""},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.SDK.name"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made with, and sit beside these, each keeping its JSON type. TelemetryDeck doesn’t index nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"type":"text","text":" holding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"type":"text","text":", and the first element of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" property is left out. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floatValue"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, becomes TelemetryDeck’s built-in parameters:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Context"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.version"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".buildNumber"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".versionAndBuildNumber"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.modelName","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.operatingSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemMajorVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemMajorMinorVersion","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.locale"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".language"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.UserPreference.region"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, the form factor and the network aren’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name or parameter name, once flattened, holds anything but ASCII letters, digits,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":", or is empty. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for one such name.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name or parameter name starts with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck."},{"text":", in any case: TelemetryDeck","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reserves that scope for its SDKs’ parameters and its server’s;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter named as one of a signal’s own members, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receivedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isTestMode"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floatValue"},{"type":"text","text":", spelled exactly so: in the flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal it would replace the member. A name like one in another case, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":", is sent."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999, which TelemetryDeck can’t parse;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 333,333 bytes. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for a signal over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the encoder’s; a third leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What TelemetryDeck doesn’t report","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck answers 200 to any namespace and any app ID it can read, so a typo in either loses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every signal without an error. Check that the first signals show up in the dashboard, in Test Mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when "},{"code":"testMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after TelemetryDeck stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and TelemetryDeck counts each copy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what TelemetryDeck receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","title":"BatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckSetupError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t be made."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydecksetuperror","title":"TelemetryDeckSetupError","kind":"symbol"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of TelemetryDeck’s Ingest API v3, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to an organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v3\/<namespace>\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","title":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}],"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"telemetryDeck"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"namespace"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"testMode"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestin